From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:07:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: free the controls after releasing the
 M2M context

Releasing the M2M context cancels both queues, and the queue cleanup
completes the requests of the buffers still queued against the
context's control handler. The handler was freed before that, so a file
closed with requests in flight completed them against freed memory.

Release the M2M context first, also in the error path of the context
setup.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c
index b4303f10c..aad81ec4a 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_context.c
@@ -808,7 +808,11 @@ int cedrus_context_setup(struct cedrus_proc *proc, struct cedrus_context *ctx,
 	return 0;
 
 error_ctrls:
+	v4l2_m2m_ctx_release(fh->m2m_ctx);
 	cedrus_context_ctrls_cleanup(ctx);
+	v4l2_fh_exit(fh);
+
+	return ret;
 
 error_v4l2_m2m:
 	v4l2_m2m_ctx_release(fh->m2m_ctx);
@@ -824,7 +828,12 @@ void cedrus_context_cleanup(struct cedrus_context *ctx, struct file *file)
 	cedrus_proc_context_active_clear(ctx->proc, ctx);
 
 	v4l2_fh_del(fh, file);
-	cedrus_context_ctrls_cleanup(ctx);
+	/*
+	 * Releasing the M2M context cancels the queues, which completes the
+	 * requests of queued buffers against the control handler: free the
+	 * controls only afterwards.
+	 */
 	v4l2_m2m_ctx_release(fh->m2m_ctx);
+	cedrus_context_ctrls_cleanup(ctx);
 	v4l2_fh_exit(fh);
 }
